{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310725,"nonce":"qcEiYHcMPI97GpfMjFGmA+KI/30=","title":"FIXED 2026-06-07 (commit 5175f2d). Root cause was a duplicate-stub registration miss in fixup_stale_cross_module_refs: when the same stdlib ...","message":"In `GenerationLoop.hx::generate`, add INSIDE the `while (true)` loop body:\n\n```haxe\nwhile (true) {\n    ...\n    step++;\n    var _t = Sys.time();   // \u003c-- this single line\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nRun canonical Paris repro. Result: program prints \"[gen] streaming...\"\n(from Main.hx, before the call to generate's loop body) then hangs\nindefinitely. Adding the Sys.time at the TOP of generate (before the\nloop) works correctly per ad38ede + feb6365.\n\n\nThe hang triggers when the source has BOTH:\n- A Sys.* call at the top of `generate()` (e.g. `Sys.getEnv` for an\n  env-controlled probe), AND\n- A Sys.* call INSIDE the loop body.\n\nEither one alone works. The combination perturbs cross-module MIR-id\nallocation enough that the `string_concat` forward-ref stub lands at\nIrFunctionId 560017 — and `install_pending_stub_safety_net` traps\nthat FuncId because the real impl maps to a different FuncId.\n\nBUT: the trap is unreachable (per `cdea22e`'s extended fixup, no\nCallDirect points at 560017 anymore). The hang persists. So the\ntrap-stub is a red herring; the actual hang is in a different code\npath.\n\n\n- **Cranelift backend stub elision** (closed by ad38ede): stub-skip\n  predicate runs; safety-net catches orphan stubs.\n- **SsaBarrier on extern Call return** (closed by feb6365): Sys.time's\n  return value gets fadd-wrap opacity for floats. Verified active\n  in the call-result path.\n- **String concat fixup** (closed by cdea22e): user-module CallDirects\n  to stale forward-ref stub ids now get name-resolved to real impls.\n\n\n**Heisenbug: ID-allocation sensitive (not egraph elaboration)**\n\nDiscriminating experiment 2026-06-07: forced `opt_level=none` in\n`CraneliftBackend::with_symbols` (cranelift_backend.rs:137) which\ndisables ALL Cranelift optimization passes including egraph\nelaboration. With opt=none + the 3-Sys.* probe: STILL HANGS. So the\nsynthesis's \"cranelift-egraph-loop-hoist\" hypothesis is REFUTED.\n\nDiscriminating experiment #2: with opt=none AND four extra\n`Sys.println(\"[bisect] ...\")` calls scattered through generate, the\nhang DISAPPEARS. With opt=speed and the same extra prints, also\nworks. So:\n\n- Hang isn't fundamental to either opt level or any specific Cranelift\n  pass.\n- Hang is HEISENBUG-sensitive to the count/shape of extern Sys.* calls\n  in the function.\n- More Sys.* calls push the MIR-id allocation past a specific\n  problematic range and the bug disappears.\n\nThis pattern is consistent with the verifier-2's framing: a `FuncId\ncollision` or fixup-coverage gap in `compile_module`, where a stub\nlands at a specific IrFunctionId (560017 was observed for\n`string_concat` in the 3-call probe), and downstream call sites still\nreach that trap-stubbed FuncId via a path the existing rewrites\n(cdea22e + ad38ede + d5f2b48) don't cover.\n\nWhat's NOT yet covered by the existing fixes:\n- vtable / fat-ptr indirect dispatch installation paths (not just\n  CallDirect / FunctionRef / MakeClosure that cdea22e handles)\n- Some MIR-level pass that captures and re-emits a stale IrFunctionId\n  reference after fixup runs (CopyPropagation? Inlining? GVN?)\n- Module-merge ordering that places the stub's id BEFORE the real\n  impl's id is registered with stdlib_function_name_map\n\n\nCLIF diff investigation (workflow `wi62x8nvo`, 2026-06-07) discovered\nthat `RAYZOR_DUMP_CLIF` dumps PRE-elaboration CLIF (the dump runs at\ncranelift_backend.rs:2169 before `module.define_function()` at\nline 2194). All three CLIF-based hypotheses (block-param mismatch,\nuse-before-def, egraph deadlock) were based on misreading the\npre-elaboration dump and are refuted.\n\n**Real next steps (priority order):**\n\n1. **Move RAYZOR_DUMP_CLIF past `module.define_function()`** so future\n   CLIF investigations actually see what runs. ~5 LOC change at\n   cranelift_backend.rs:2169-2185. Code-hygiene improvement orthogonal\n   to this specific bug.\n\n2. **Capture FuncId → name map under both 3-Sys.* (hang) and 7-Sys.*\n   (works) configurations.** Diff to see what functions land at\n   IrFunctionId 560000-560020 in each case. The bug likely lives in\n   that range's installation.\n\n3. **Run with `sample \u003cpid\u003e`** while hung to get the runtime PC. If\n   it's inside JIT pages → JIT compile somehow corrupted; if inside\n   `librayzor_runtime` → runtime path. The CLIF data alone can't\n   distinguish.\n\n4. **Check fixup pass coverage of vtable / fat-ptr indirect paths.**\n   cdea22e's extended fixup covers CallDirect / FunctionRef /\n   MakeClosure but does NOT walk vtable installation sites or\n   indirect-call patches. If string_concat (or whatever lands at the\n   bad id) gets called via vtable lookup, the trap-stub installed by\n   the safety-net at finalize() fires.\n\nEstimated effort: 2-4 hours (deeper investigation than first thought).\n\n\nPer the standing workaround documented in\n[[bugs-sys-call-in-generation-method]]: read Sys-side values in\n`nue.Main.main` (where they work), thread through the constructor.\nDon't call Sys.* methods in the body of `generate()`.\n\nFor perf profiling: use the runtime-side `kernel_timing` module\n(landed 92010bd) which doesn't touch the Haxe source at all, sidestepping\nthe bug entirely.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_sys_call_in_loop_body_open` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}